{"help_t", "Help"},
{"packs_title", "InkPeek language packs"},
{"hp_get_t", "Getting packs"},
{"help_dict_t", "Dictionary"},
{"help_dict", "Wiktionary articles in the answer language (via kaikki.org); English words also from the translation tables of the English Wiktionary; WikDict where Wiktionary has no article. The first line: the word with its grammar and the main meanings."},
{"help_gram_t", "Grammar"},
{"help_gram", "Gender, plural, verb forms, irregular or strong — from Wiktionary's inflection tables. Every form leads to its word: Häusern → Haus, went → go. Only what Wiktionary says, no guessing."},
{"help_build_t", "Build"},
{"help_build", "Our scripts on GitHub build every pack from these open sources and check it with tests (words and their forms) before publishing; the app downloads only from the project's releases."},
{"help_labels", "Each pair has a label: full — the dictionary knows 85 % or more of the 5,000 most frequent words, and offline translation is there; basic — 60 % or more; experimental — less."},
{"hm_fast", "Mozilla's models, through English: fast, any device, about 30 MB per direction. The meaning comes through; informal and formal you (du/Sie), gender and turns of phrase may get lost."},
{"hm_opus", "Straight between the languages, no English in between: closer to the original. About 170 MB per model, 4 GB of memory."},
{"hm_llm", "An AI model on the device (Tencent Hy-MT2, 1.1 GB): the most natural, but slow; needs 6 GB of memory and an int8-capable CPU."},
{"hm_off", "No offline translation: Translate shows AI only, a phrase opens on word by word."},
{"help_lid_t", "Language of the text"},
{"help_lid", "fastText (lid.176); when it is unsure (a word or two), the dictionary that knows more of the words decides."},
{"own_title", "StarDict dictionaries"},
{"help_other_t", "Other dictionaries"},
{"help_other", "Any StarDict dictionary, the format KOReader, GoldenDict and ColorDict use: download one from WikDict, Wiktionary or FreeDict, import files, or point the app to a folder. In the card they come after the packs by default (Card → Article → Dictionary order); each line is signed with its name."},
{"help_formats_t", "Import"},
{"help_formats", "Pick the dictionary's files together (.ifo, .idx or .idx.gz, .dict or .dict.dz, .syn if there is one) or one archive: zip, tar, tar.gz, tar.bz2, tar.xz, tar.zst. Every dictionary in it gets its own folder."},
{"help_folder_t", "Folder"},
{"aih_what_t", "What AI adds"},
{"aih_what", "Optional tabs on top of the offline core: AI translation, Analysis and Context. Dictionary, grammar and offline translation never need it; with AI off its tabs are gone."},
{"aih_translate", "A word: its base form, gender, forms and main meanings; a phrase or passage: a natural translation that keeps the sentence type. Without a network Translate shows the offline translation."},
{"aih_analysis", "Grammar: which form it is, how it is built and the rule behind it. Words: the harder words, or synonyms and related ones."},
{"aih_context", "Explanation: what it means here, register, idioms, nuances. Examples: three everyday sentences with a translation."},
{"aih_keys_t", "Key"},
{"aih_local_t", "Own server"},
{"aih_local", "LM Studio, Ollama, llama.cpp, vLLM and other servers with the OpenAI API: choose a preset and change the IP. No cloud, no key; the answer may take longer."},
{"aih_free_t", "Free"},
{"aih_free", "OpenRouter has free models: open the model list and turn on Free only. Free models are slower and change often."},
{"aih_send_t", "What is sent"},
{"hn_ai_t", "AI"},
{"hn_dl_t", "Downloads"},
{"hn_dl", "Packs, models and other dictionaries are downloaded only when you ask: from the project's GitHub releases (models also from their original site) and the dictionary sources you pick."},
{"ht_notes", "Notes"},
{"hw_save_t", "Saving"},
{"hw_save", "☆ in the card saves a word as its base form (Häusern → Haus), a phrase as it is. A filled star: saved already."},
{"hw_hist_t", "History"},
{"hw_hist", "Everything you open, the last 1,000, with how many times you looked each up; an entry keeps its AI answers, so it opens offline later. Card → Opening → History turns it off."},
{"hw_del_t", "Removing"},
{"hw_del", "✕ removes one entry, Clear history the whole history; what is saved stays."},
{"hw_anki_t", "Anki"},
{"hw_backup_t", "Export and import"},
{"hw_daily_t", "Daily copies"},
{"hs_start_t", "Getting started"},
{"hs_access_t", "Accessibility"},
{"hs_access", "LexiPeek reads the selected text through macOS Accessibility: allow it once in System Settings → Privacy & Security → Accessibility. Nothing leaves this Mac for it, and the clipboard is never touched."},
{"hs_keys_t", "Hotkeys"},
{"hs_keys", "Select text in any app and press {1}: the card opens under it. {2} opens a card to type in. Both can be changed in Settings → General; there, apps where they should do nothing can be listed."},
{"hs_icon_t", "Icon at the selection"},
{"hs_icon", "Card → Opening → Icon at the selection: after you select text with the mouse, a small icon appears next to it; a click opens the card. It goes after a few seconds."},
{"hs_other_t", "Other ways in"},
{"hs_other", "The context menu's Services → {1} (no Accessibility needed), the LexiPeek window (menu bar → Open LexiPeek) and links lexipeek://lookup?text=… (PopClip, scripts)."},
{"hc_card_t", "The card"},
{"hc_kinds_t", "Word, phrase, passage"},
{"hc_kinds", "A word opens on Dictionary: its header with grammar, then each dictionary's line. A phrase (up to 8 words) opens on its translation, word by word on Dictionary. A passage shows its translation. The badge (de → ru) is a menu: another language of the text or another answer language."},
{"hc_nav_t", "Going deeper"},
{"hc_nav", "A click on a word of a phrase or a section opens it in the same card, ← comes back. A dictionary's line opens its full entry with senses, examples and sections (related words, synonyms, forms); with full entries ◀ ▶ go from one dictionary to the next. A cut header opens whole on a click."},
{"hc_bar_t", "The bottom row"},
{"hc_bar", "The translation method (its tooltip: how long it took), copy, the badge, ☆ (saves to Notes) and the pin: a pinned card stays open; a dragged one can stay too (Card → Opening)."},
{"hc_keys_t", "Keys in the card"},
{"hc_keys", "←/→ switch tabs, Delete or ⌘[ goes back, ⌘S is ☆, ⌘P pins, Esc or a click elsewhere closes the card."},
{"hp_get_d", "Settings → Languages → Packs lists the pairs; a pair brings its dictionary, grammar and offline translation. Download, Update (when the release has newer files) and ⋯ → Remove (what no other pair needs)."},
{"ho_folder", "Imported and downloaded dictionaries go into LexiPeek's own folder; folders of other apps (KOReader's, GoldenDict's) can be added and are read in place, never written."},
{"ha_when", "AI tabs ask only when you open them (or a phrase opens on one: Card → Opening). With \"Ask the other AI tabs at once\" (AI → Modules) the others are ready when you open them. A module with nothing ticked has no tab and sends nothing."},
{"ha_keys", "The API key is kept in the macOS Keychain, one per provider; it is given to a request and never goes to settings, logs, the screen or exports. Claude Code and Codex use their own login instead."},
{"hn_ai_d", "Only when you open an AI tab, or a phrase opens on one (Card → Opening): the selected text and the answer language go to the provider you chose. Nothing else from this Mac. Answers are kept here."},
{"hw_anki_d", "TSV… under a list saves it for Anki or a spreadsheet: text, meaning, AI translation, language, date — Anki imports it as is."},
{"hw_backup_d", "Export… saves everything (saved, history, AI answers) as one file; Import… adds from such a file what this Mac does not have. InkPeek's backups import too, and the other way round."},
{"hw_daily_d", "A copy of everything is made each day in LexiPeek's folder → backup, the last five kept: to go back to one, Import it."},
{"help_menu", "LexiPeek Help"},
{"help_open", "Open {1}"},
{"net_offline", "No network: check the connection."},
{"net_unreachable", "The server does not answer: check the network or the VPN, then try again."},
{"mt_ask_ai", "Translate with AI…"},
{"ai_title_on", "Its tabs in the card and AI translation: AI → Modules. Off: everything works offline."},
{"no_apps", "No apps yet."},
{"ai_open_settings", "Open Settings → AI"},
