{"icon_d@win", "A small icon next to a new selection opens the card. Read through UI Automation; the clipboard is not touched."},
{"login_d@win", "LexiPeek starts with Windows, in the notification area."},
{"show_finder@win", "Show in Explorer"},
{"key_saved@win", "Kept in the Windows Credential Manager ✓"},
{"key_missing@win", "No key yet: paste it here; it is kept in the Windows Credential Manager, never in the settings."},
{"ai_cli_d@win", "Its name or full path; it runs on this computer with its own login."},
{"hs_access_t@win", "Reading the selection"},
{"hs_access@win", "LexiPeek reads the selected text through Windows UI Automation: nothing to allow. An app that does not show its selection gets a card with a field to type in. Nothing leaves this computer for it, and the clipboard is never touched."},
{"hs_other@win", "The LexiPeek window (the tray icon → Open LexiPeek): type or paste a text there."},
{"hc_keys@win", "←/→ switch tabs, Backspace goes back, Ctrl+S is ☆, Ctrl+P pins, Esc or a click elsewhere closes the card."},
{"ha_keys@win", "The API key is kept in the Windows Credential Manager, one per provider; it is given to a request and never goes to settings, logs, the screen or exports. Claude Code and Codex use their own login instead."},
